invariant: INV-58
file: p256_sign.c
catches: p256_sign_fault_test
reason: write_if_checked copies the candidate to sig before it reads the
  checks' verdict, so a signature that failed a check is in the caller's
  buffer when the call returns 0. A caller that ignores the return value
  sends it. bin/p256_sign_fault_test requires every byte of sig as it was
  after each refused fault.

--- old
    int fits = candidate_len <= cap;
--- new
    int fits = candidate_len <= cap;
    if (fits) {
        memcpy(sig, candidate, candidate_len);
    }
